Ladybird queues a VisibilityStateEntry with a timestamp of 0 when a
document’s initial visibility state is set, and another stamped with
the current time on each change, and buffers up to 50 of them. Blink
does the same in WindowPerformance::AddVisibilityStateEntry(): Its
constructor calls that with a null timestamp for the page’s initial
visibility, and WindowPerformance::PageVisibilityChangedWithTimestamp()
calls it for each change, up to kDefaultVisibilityStateEntrySize (50)
entries. WebKit and Gecko don’t implement VisibilityStateEntry.
